<title>AUSTRALIA: FORECAST-Australian interest rates poll - June.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Australian interest rates poll - June.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) board met on Tuesday for its monthly meeting.</p>
<p>Ahead of the meeting 27 economists were asked one question -- the percentage chance of another cut in official interest rates this cycle following the 0.5 percentage point surprise easing to 5.5 percent on May 23.</p>
<p>The median is below 50 percent, but there are a few economists at, or above, 50 percent. Some at around 40 percent said the bias to their forecasts was to the topside, and the activity data over the next few months would be the key. ----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>		Percent chance</p>
<p>		 of rate cut </p>
<p>ABN		 40</p>
<p>Access	     5</p>
<p>AMP		 45</p>
<p>ANZ Bank	  25</p>
<p>ANZ Secs	  40</p>
<p>Axiom	     25</p>
<p>BT		  30-40</p>
<p>BZW		 10-15</p>
<p>Citibank	  less than 50</p>
<p>Col State	 60</p>
<p>Comm Bank	 25</p>
<p>County	    10</p>
<p>DMG		 n/a*</p>
<p>Dresdner	  40</p>
<p>HSBC		20</p>
<p>Hambros	   35</p>
<p>JP Morgan	 50</p>
<p>Macquarie	 30</p>
<p>Merrills	  40</p>
<p>NAB		 10</p>
<p>Nomura	    40</p>
<p>Pru Bache	 40</p>
<p>Rothschild	30</p>
<p>SBC Warburg     50</p>
<p>Soc Gen	   30</p>
<p>UBS		 20 </p>
<p>Westpac	   50 </p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Low	    5</p>
<p>    High	  60</p>
<p>    Average     32</p>
<p>    Median	35</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    *DMG forecast was for a &quot;good&quot; chance for a rate cut.</p>
<p>    -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800 (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
